%% Four parties: the Operator Workspace, @ranza/business-day, PostgreSQL and
%% apps/worker. Both paths end in the same insert, stamped by the same trigger,
%% so a manual close and an automatic one cannot record different things.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor SM as Staff Member
  participant WS as Operator Workspace
  participant BD as @ranza/business-day
  participant PG as PostgreSQL
  participant WK as apps/worker

  rect rgb(240, 248, 246)
  note over SM,PG: s1, close a day by hand (ranza_app, request context)
  SM->>WS: open close-day?property=P
  WS->>BD: getCloseTheDay(user, P)
  BD->>PG: day to close, backlog, open items, Folios left open, recent closes
  PG-->>BD: rows the viewer's policies let through
  BD-->>WS: the checklist
  SM->>WS: Close D, with a reason when items are open
  WS->>BD: closeDay(user, P, D, reason)
  BD->>PG: pg_advisory_xact_lock(3, P)
  BD->>PG: insert business_day_closes (organization, P, D, reason)
  PG->>PG: stamped (definer trigger): caller check, D before today, D-1 closed,<br/>counts and open items computed, a reason when any are open
  PG->>PG: policy: capability front_desk and front_desk.close_day
  BD->>PG: outbox business_day.closed, audit business_day.closed
  PG-->>BD: committed, or 23505 already closed, 55000 / 23514 not closable
  BD-->>WS: closed, or why not
  end

  rect rgb(246, 244, 240)
  note over WK,PG: s2, the worker closes a quiet day (ranza_worker)
  WK->>BD: closeDueDays() every 60 s, one pass at a time
  BD->>PG: app.properties_due_for_close()
  PG-->>BD: (organization, P, D) where D is the next due day
  loop each due Property, its own transaction
    BD->>PG: app.set_worker_context(organization, business_day.close)
    BD->>PG: app.close_business_day_automatically(P, D)
    PG->>PG: lock 3, open items? then insert, same trigger, closed_by_job set
    PG-->>BD: closed, open_items, already_closed or unavailable
  end
  BD-->>WK: report: due, closed, open, failed
  end
